{"company":{"ticker":"MU","name":"Micron Technology","sector":"Technology","industry":"Semiconductors","size":"large","cik":723125},"scores":{"growth":99.0,"quality":69.0,"value":69.0,"acceleration":100.0,"price_momentum":70.0,"reality":90.0,"pricing":50.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"MU","opportunity_score":73.0,"components":{"structural_trend":57.0,"capital_flow":76.0,"acceleration":100.0,"quality":69.0,"valuation":69.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":81.0,"narrative":69.0,"pricing":52.0,"expectations_gap":29.0,"macro_fit":53.0,"sector_rotation":66.0,"theme_pricing":57.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth +167.0% vs +85.5% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +1291.4%, FCF margin +29.0%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"ROIC +74.5%, incremental ROIC +176.7%"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +65.6% (+4304 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":false,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 57.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":true,"evidence":"Technology rotation score +66"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":true,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 69.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":true,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 69.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA -0.3"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":false,"evidence":"Diluted share count +1.1% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Micron Technology (MU) screens at opportunity 73.0 with an expectations gap of 29.0. Reality 81.0 reflects +167.0% TTM revenue growth, +65.6% operating margin and +74.5% ROIC; pricing 52.0 reflects a fair multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Infrastructure (trend 56.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced roughly in line with its own history and peers; the market expects the current trajectory to continue.","evidence":["EV/Sales 13.3x (77.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 24x (10.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 2.1%","PEG 0.0","12m return +549%, -11% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (81.0) is running ahead of what is priced (52.0): an expectations gap of +29 pts.","Revenue growth is accelerating (+167.0% TTM, +81.4 pts) while the multiple has not re-rated.","Operating leverage is showing up in margins faster than in the valuation."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-06-25)","AI Infrastructure: evidence that 'GPU supply, power availability, cooling, network bandwidth' is easing via Accelerators, optical/electrical interconnect, HBM memory, liquid cooling, on-site power","Edge AI: evidence that 'Power-efficient silicon, on-device memory' is easing via NPUs in phones/PCs/cars, low-power memory","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 117% (currently 167.0%)","ROIC falls below 56% (currently 74.5%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 65.6%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Infrastructure theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":1.1689,"current":1.6698},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.5586,"current":0.7448},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.4303681649003577},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":66.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":64.5},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Infrastructure theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-infrastructure","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":56.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-infrastructure","theme":"AI Infrastructure","weight":0.7,"order":1,"effective":0.7},{"theme_id":"edge-ai","theme":"Edge AI","weight":0.2,"order":2,"effective":0.12}],"llm":{"thesis":"Micron is in the steepest up-leg of a memory cycle that has been supercharged by AI: TTM revenue +167% to $90.3B, operating margin 65.6% (+4,304 bps YoY), ROIC 74.5% and net cash of $20.3B. The engine reads reality 81 vs pricing 52 and calls a +29pt expectations gap, largely because P/E sits at 24x (10th percentile of its own 5-year history). I think that specific input is the weakest link: memory stocks are always optically cheapest on trailing earnings at the peak, and the market's real vote is EV/Sales at 13.3x \u2014 the 77th percentile of history and roughly 1.5x the 8.9x median \u2014 which says the market already capitalizes a structurally higher-margin HBM franchise, not a trough. The investable edge is therefore not 'cheap stock,' it is duration: if HBM contracts, three-player supply discipline and AI capex hold gross margin above 60% for another 4-6 quarters, the multiple is defensible and the stock compounds with earnings; if pricing rolls, the 24x becomes 8x on halved EPS. Own it as a high-conviction, high-beta cyclical with tight break conditions, not as a value re-rating.","fundamental_read":"The operating numbers are exceptional and are accelerating, not decelerating: revenue growth went from +85.5% to +167.0%, incremental ROIC is 177%, and net income grew 7.1x \u2014 this is a pure price/mix-driven memory upcycle where nearly all incremental revenue drops through. Cash generation is real but capex-heavy: OCF $51.4B against $25.3B capex leaves $26.2B FCF, a 52% conversion rate, so the FCF yield (2.1%) is half the earnings yield (4.1%) and will stay compressed while HBM and leading-edge DRAM capacity is built. The balance sheet is a genuine asset \u2014 net debt/EBITDA -0.3x, interest coverage 258x \u2014 which means Micron can keep spending through a downturn rather than be forced to cut into it. Shareholder return is negligible ($650M buybacks, $567M dividends, ~0.1% shareholder yield) against 1.1% dilution, so all value creation currently depends on the capex paying off.","technical_read":"The trend is unambiguously intact: close $1,080.53 above the 20/50/200-day (986.8/937.0/656.9), a 50>200 uptrend, RSI 63 and positive MACD histogram. But the stock sits 64.5% above its 200-day and +549% over 12 months, which is an extension level that historically precedes violent mean-reversion; the -11% 3-month return against +15.8% in the last month suggests a high-level consolidation that has resolved upward rather than a top. Key levels: the 52-week high ~11% above, and the 50-day near $937 as first structural support \u2014 a sustained close below the 200-day (~$657) would be a regime change, not a dip.","market_expectation":"At 13.3x EV/Sales (77th percentile) and 17.6x EV/EBITDA on peak-cycle EBITDA, the market is not pricing a trough multiple on peak earnings \u2014 it is pricing that a large share of today's ~65% operating margin is structural, i.e. that HBM is a contracted, share-allocated, AI-linked business rather than a commodity. Implicitly consensus expects several more quarters of tight supply, continued AI accelerator build-out pulling HBM3E/HBM4, and no return to the 2023-style oversupply. The 24x P/E is not a cheapness signal; it is the arithmetic of trailing EPS of $44.17 that the market does not believe is a permanent run-rate.","what_market_misses":["The engine's 'cheapness vs history 69' is driven by P/E (10th pct) and EV/EBITDA (5th pct) \u2014 both trailing-earnings measures that systematically mislead on memory at cycle peaks. EV/Sales at the 77th percentile is the contradicting, and more honest, signal; the +29pt expectations gap is likely overstated.","Conversely, what may be genuinely under-appreciated is mix durability rather than magnitude: HBM is sold on long-dated agreements and consumes 2-3x the wafer supply per bit of standard DRAM, which structurally tightens conventional DDR5/LPDDR supply as a side effect \u2014 the commodity leg of the business may stay tight even if HBM pricing normalizes.","Capital intensity is the hidden variable. FCF conversion of 52% means reported earnings materially overstate distributable cash; a bull case requires capex to plateau, and no evidence here shows it will.","Net cash of $20.3B in a capital-intensive cyclical is a competitive weapon that valuation frameworks ignore \u2014 it funds counter-cyclical capacity while levered peers retrench.","Coverage is only 0.75: estimate revisions, guidance and insider/institutional flow are not connected. For a stock whose thesis is entirely about forward pricing, the missing estimate-revision feed is the single most important absent input."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-06-25 filing): HBM sold-out commentary, FY capex guide, and any bit-supply-growth discipline signal.","Confirmation of HBM4 qualification/allocation with major accelerator customers and multi-year pricing agreements.","Evidence that AI infrastructure bottlenecks (power, cooling, interconnect) are easing, which would sustain accelerator shipment growth and therefore HBM attach.","Edge AI inflection: on-device LPDDR content growth in phones/PCs/autos broadening demand beyond datacenter.","Continued Technology sector rotation (+66, by far the strongest of 11 sectors) and any shift toward a capex-friendly Reflation regime.","Initiation of a materially larger buyback once capex plateaus \u2014 would convert the net-cash balance sheet into per-share value and offset the 1.1% dilution."],"risks":["Peak-cycle earnings risk: at 65.6% operating margin, the downside asymmetry is severe \u2014 memory margins have historically gone negative, and a 24x P/E on peak EPS offers no protection.","Supply response: three-player discipline is a behavioral assumption, not a structural one. Competitor HBM capacity additions and conventional DRAM wafer restarts could flip pricing within two quarters.","AI capex digestion by hyperscalers \u2014 the demand side is concentrated in a handful of buyers whose order patterns can turn abruptly.","Extension risk: 64.5% above the 200-day after a +549% 12-month move means positioning is crowded and drawdowns will be non-linear.","Capital intensity: $25.3B capex is committed years ahead of the revenue it serves; a demand air pocket lands on a fixed cost base.","Macro regime is barely differentiated (Goldilocks 26.6% vs Contraction 25.4%, Stagflation 23.5%) \u2014 there is no real macro tailwind here, only sector rotation.","Geopolitical/China exposure and export-control changes are structural overhangs for memory that this evidence set does not quantify."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below ~117% (currently 167.0%) \u2014 the first sign the price-driven leg is rolling.","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 65.6%) or gross margin drops below 60%.","ROIC falls below 56% (currently 74.5%) or incremental ROIC turns negative.","EV/Sales pushes above roughly 16x without a corresponding step-up in contracted HBM revenue \u2014 pure multiple expansion on peak fundamentals.","Capex guided materially above $25.3B while revenue growth decelerates \u2014 the classic memory over-build signal.","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66).","Price closes >10% below the 200-day average with negative relative strength; a loss of the 50-day near $937 is the early warning.","AI Infrastructure theme trend drops below 45 (currently 56.0) or adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently ~48.9%)."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Wafer fab equipment vendors \u2014 Micron's $25.3B capex is direct revenue for deposition, etch, and lithography suppliers; DRAM-leveraged toolmakers capture the spend whether or not Micron's margin holds.","Advanced packaging and TSV/hybrid-bonding equipment and test houses \u2014 HBM stacking is yield-limited, so packaging capacity and high-bandwidth memory testers are the true bottleneck and command scarcity pricing.","ABF substrate, interposer and materials suppliers feeding HBM+accelerator co-packaging.","Fab construction, electrical contracting and industrial gas suppliers serving greenfield US fab builds.","Power and thermal infrastructure providers \u2014 HBM-dense accelerators raise rack power density, pulling demand for liquid cooling, high-density power delivery and on-site generation.","Competing memory suppliers and NAND players \u2014 the shortage Micron's HBM wafer conversion creates in conventional DRAM lifts the whole complex's pricing.","Negatively: PC, smartphone and server OEMs, for whom Micron's pricing power is a direct bill-of-materials cost increase and a margin transfer."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue $90.27B, +167.0% YoY, with operating margin 65.6% and ROIC 74.5% as of period ending 2026-05-28.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Net debt is -$20.3B (net cash), net debt/EBITDA -0.3x, interest coverage 258x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E 24.2x sits at the 10th percentile of its own 5-year history while EV/Sales 13.3x sits at the 77th percentile.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"FCF $26.2B on OCF $51.4B and capex $25.3B; FCF conversion 52%, FCF yield 2.1%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Stock is +549% over 12 months, 64.5% above its 200-day, RSI 63, -11% from the 52-week high.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market expects the current AI-driven memory pricing trajectory to persist, per the deterministic engine summary.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"The low trailing P/E reflects peak-cycle earnings rather than genuine cheapness; EV/Sales at the 77th percentile is the more reliable read of what is priced.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The engine's +29pt expectations gap is likely overstated because its valuation component leans on trailing-earnings multiples that mislead for memory cyclicals.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Low FCF conversion means reported earnings overstate distributable cash and the bull case requires a capex plateau.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"HBM wafer conversion structurally tightens conventional DDR5/LPDDR supply, extending the pricing cycle beyond datacenter demand alone.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Advanced packaging and HBM test capacity, not wafer capacity, is the binding constraint and the most attractive second-order profit pool.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"A materially larger buyback follows a capex plateau and becomes the next re-rating catalyst.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.55}},"technical":{"score":100,"passes":8,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":true,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":true,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":true},"ready":true,"stage":"stage2_uptrend","close":1080.53,"sma50":937.03,"sma150":762.23,"sma200":656.92,"sma150_prev4w":684.84,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":589.0,"pct_from_52w_high":-11.0,"rs_6m":185.1,"rsi14":63.0,"atr20":44.768,"atr_pct":4.14,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-05-28","filed":"2026-06-25","revenue":90274000000.0,"gross_profit":65511000000.0,"operating_income":59243000000.0,"net_income":50469000000.0,"ebitda":68254000000.0,"ocf":51432000000.0,"capex":25260000000.0,"fcf":26172000000.0,"eps":44.17,"shares_diluted":1138750000.0,"cash":26022000000.0,"debt":5722000000.0,"net_debt":-20300000000.0,"equity":100724000000.0,"total_assets":134112000000.0,"rnd":4784000000.0,"sbc":1184000000.0,"buybacks":650000000.0,"dividends":567000000.0,"gross_margin":0.7256906750559408,"operating_margin":0.6562576157033033,"net_margin":0.5590646254735583,"fcf_margin":0.2899173626957928,"fcf_conversion":0.5185757593770434,"revenue_growth":1.6698015556147046,"revenue_growth_prev":0.8554736136385404,"revenue_acceleration":0.8143279419761642,"eps_growth":6.929982046678637,"net_income_growth":7.107469879518073,"fcf_growth":12.913875598086124,"operating_margin_change":0.4303681649003577,"roic":0.7448001579418101,"incremental_roic":1.7672151835775107,"operating_income_estimated":false,"financial":false,"roe":0.5010623088836822,"roa":0.3763197924123121,"net_debt_to_ebitda":-0.2974184663169924,"interest_coverage":257.5782608695652,"dilution":0.011098779134295134,"sbc_pct_revenue":0.01311562576157033,"tax_rate":0.14572328321820